Package: migrator
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, awk, bash (>= 4.4), coreutils, gzip,
 openssh-client, tar, util-linux
Recommends: migrator-agent (= ${source:Version}), partclone, e2fsprogs,
 initramfs-tools, lz4, mdadm, lvm2, xfsprogs, zstd
Suggests: gdisk, grub2-common, parted, pv, qemu-system-x86, qemu-utils,
 rsync, tmux
Description: move a running Linux server onto this machine over the network
 migrator copies a whole Linux installation from a donor machine onto the
 machine it runs on, then reboots the copy. It reads both sides, writes a
 migration plan that can be inspected and edited, recreates the donor's disk
 layout on the target, streams every file system, repairs the copy in a chroot
 (fstab, initramfs drivers, boot loader, network) and verifies that the result
 boots before the switch-over.
 .
 Two modes are supported. Off-line, both machines run the migration Live and
 the donor is read only. On-line, the donor keeps running: the volumes are
 copied in passes by migrator-agent, then frozen for a last delta, which keeps
 the outage to the time it takes to write the remaining differences.
 .
 The tool needs root, because it partitions disks and mounts file systems. It
 is normally run from the migration Live, which ships with everything it needs;
 this package is for building that Live and for hosts that prepare a plan
 without writing anything.

Package: migrator-agent
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: on-line migration agent for migrator
 migrator-agent is the half that runs on the donor during an on-line migration.
 It tracks block writes, serves the frozen volume over the connection migrator
 opens, and reports the progress of each pass back to the driver.
 .
 It is a statically linked binary so that nothing has to be installed on the
 donor: migrator copies it into a tmpfs under /run and starts it there. It is
 not meant to be started by hand.
